{
  "title": "Function notation",
  "subject": "Math",
  "grade": "9-10",
  "learningGoal": "Evaluate f(x) at specific inputs.",
  "spokenLines": [
    "Function notation. f of x. Read that as \"f of x.\"",
    "It means: give me an input, I'll give you an output.",
    "Say f of x equals two x plus one.",
    "What's f of three? Plug three in for x.",
    "Two times three plus one is seven.",
    "So f of three equals seven.",
    "f of zero? Two times zero plus one, which is one.",
    "Same rule, just swap what you plug in."
  ],
